<title>LATVIA: FLIGHTS TO BEGIN FROM LIEPAJA TO MOSCOW - REPORT.</title>
<headline>FLIGHTS TO BEGIN FROM LIEPAJA TO MOSCOW - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Russian company is planning to start flights from the port town of Liepaja to Moscow, newspaper Dienas Bizness said on Friday.</p>
<p>It quoted the head of the Liepaja Air Company, Arturs Kokars, as saying that a Russian state transport company Rossija would use a Yak 40 to make the flights on Monday and Friday morning to Vnukovo airport, starting June 20.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
